Independent Luna review and primary-agent integration record

Measurement methodology
The independent reviewer checked the fixed 32 production plus eight A/A
schedule, balanced handler/filesystem orders, pinned inputs, fail-fast run
behavior, same-handler controls and scoped disposable-image cleanup. The
review identified the obsolete fail-open snapdog-runner.service guard and
missing complete Workbench receipts. Root retained actual loaded/inactive
GitHub/GitLab unit states, checked for active GitHub runner processes, and
later compared all 67 non-handler installed asset receipts across 40 runs.
The exact originally executed script is unchanged and its SHA256 is retained.

Scope and parser
The reviewer checked that sparse directory-read CRC can be reached in create
and the initial open of grow-new-file phases, but ordinary writes/file data
are unchanged and timings do not attribute CRC work. The initial A/A summary
pooled normal/durable controls; the author added within-mode aggregates and
a divergent-mode oracle. The mixed statistics are separately labeled.
Root clarified that default local summary invocation follows raw collection
from Cachy's separate result root. The independent reviewer found the final
strict schedule, exact 23 phases, binary/RDB checks and pair semantics sound.

