Tests and setup correction
An early reviewer counted17 tests while root's file and actual log showed18;
the within-mode oracle made19 summary tests. Root's final combined execution
has24 tests (19 summary plus five asset receipts), all PASS; the separately
reused parser has25 PASS. Actual execution logs are authoritative, not a
manual method count. Root's first asset-test import failed because the helper
was named verify-assets.py; the module was renamed verify_assets.py without
changing tests, input receipts or timings. The failed log is retained.

Final consistency review
The independent reviewer read the complete report, new HANDOFF section, plan
decision, evidence README, asset verifier and tests. It found no actionable
inconsistencies in the checked claims: numerical medians/read-control cautions,
provisional status, separate open performance goal, corrected5x threshold,
disclosed import failure and no new core qualification. No reviewer launched
benchmarks, changed measured source, dispatched CI or modified GitHub state.
